title: lore_listener_hall
---
Stone: "Here we gathered to listen to the Earth herself sing."
Stone: The carving continues, weathered: "And she sang back."
===

title: lore_first_note
---
Stone: "This spire holds the first note. Strike it and the others answer."
Stone: A small diagram shows three buildings arrayed in a triangle, lines of light running between them.
===

title: lore_thread_memory
---
Stone: "The water remembers names the wind forgot."
Stone: Below, an etched list of names, half-eroded. You don't recognize any of them.
===

title: lore_old_well
---
Stone: "Drop a stone. Listen. The well replies in 432 Hz."
Stone: A child's hand, perhaps, has scratched a smaller note: "tried this — it works"
===

title: lore_broken_gate
---
Stone: "They came in floods. We left in song."
Stone: There are scorch marks across the lower carving. Not from fire — something stranger.
===

title: lore_root_chamber
---
Stone: "Aether wells up where the roots go deepest."
Stone: An arrow points downward. You feel a low pulse through your feet, like a slow heartbeat.
===
